            "value": [
              {
                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "<p>Code that was used for the simulations for the paper \"NetSquid, a discrete-event simulation platform for quantum networks\" (https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.12535).</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This file contains four compressed tarballs (tar.gz files), each containing code for the simulation of a particular use case:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><code>quantum_switch_code</code>: a quantum switch (see sec. IIB in the paper and plots therein)</li>\r\n<li><code>nv_repeater_chain_code</code>: nitrogen-vacancy based repeater chain (sec. IIC)</li>\r\n<li><code>ae_repeater_code</code>: atomic-ensemble based repeater (sec. IID)</li>\r\n<li><code>benchmarking_code</code>: benchmarking NetSquid's runtime</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>For installation and use of the code, please see the READMEs in the individual zip files.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Copyright TNO and TU Delft (QuTech).</p>"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
